$var1 100
$var2 -20

:begin
	fadeto black 0
	justify centre
	pos 0 150
	size 48
	msg "THE CLOSET\nBy Audrey Castillo\nClick to begin"
	waitkey
	jump story

:story
	msg " "
	fadeto transparent 5
	justify left
	pos 16 32
	size 24
	bg closet
	playsound "event:/Music" 0
	wait 5

	msg "I'm sitting in my closet. Hiding from it."
	waitkey
	append "\nI know it's just out there. Waiting for me."
	waitkey

	msg "It all started three weeks ago when I let it in, on what was supposed to be just a regular day."
	waitkey
	append " Out doing my shopping, I never suspected..."
	waitkey

	playsound "event:/Knocking"
	wait 1.5
	msg "It's just out there! I must tell my story quickly so whoever finds me can know the truth."
	waitkey

	// Have a fade to a shopping background here

	msg "Outside the store, the strange figures were handing out flyers. I wouldn't normally pay them a second thought, but one of them was unusually pushy."
	waitkey
	append "\n\n\"Hello! You look in need of a friend. Please take a moment to read through this. It may be your salvation.\""
	waitkey
	append "\n\nI offered a polite smile but declined."
	waitkey
	append " The woman's face instantly turned dark."
	waitkey

	msg "\"I know the look behind your eyes. You are lonely. We see it all the time. The world can be a harsh, empty place without companionship. Please... take a look.\""
	waitkey
	append "\n\nI hesitated. She wasn't wrong -- I had just moved to this town not long ago and hadn't made any friends yet. My life *was* quite lonely."
	waitkey
	append "\n\n\I accepted the flyer, not expecting much. I didn't even look at it until it tumbled out of the shopping bag I hastily shoved it into when I arrived home."
	waitkey

	// Inside home background (maybe picture of the flyer?)

	msg "Round pets! Long pets! Noisy pets! Cuddly pets! All for $50!"
	append "\n\nThe flyer was decorated with frankly amateurish drawings of... creatures. Dogs? Horses? It was hard to tell. They looked as if they were drawn by children who had never seen another living creature."
	waitkey
	append " The vagueness about what *animals* were available made it even stranger. This kind of thing would normally specify \"dogs or cats for adoption\", right?"
	waitkey

	msg "Even so, the thought of a pet was a comforting one. Before I moved I had enjoyed the company of my parents' dog named Cookie. I had also noticed that on my rental agreement that pets *were* allowed with prior approval."
	waitkey
	append " I let the idea sit with me for a few days, most of which were occupied by time at work, commuting to work or commuting *from* work. A few lonely days that ended with me crawling into bed, exhausted and alone, only to wake up the next morning and repeat the routine."
	waitkey
	append " Maybe a pet wasn't such a bad idea."
	waitkey

	// factories background

	msg "So the next day I had free, I drove to the address the flyer had listed. It was somewhat outside of town, down a quiet road through the industrial area. Unassuming, even more so as the rain fell heavy and forced me to slow down in the poor visibility."
	append " I should have stayed away."
	waitkey

	msg "As the car pulled up to the delapidated weatherboard shack, things seemed wrong. No one else parked in the carpark, not even staff."
	waitkey
	append " The lights off, yet the "open" sign glowing brightly in neon through the fog. But the loneliness ate away at me. Maybe they were closed and forgot to turn the sign off?"
	waitkey
	append " Stupidly, I persisted."
	waitkey
	playsound "event:/Knocking"

	msg "After parking and locking up, I headed inside -- to my surprise -- as the door was unlocked. A tiny lobby stood before me, along with a strange smell I struggle to recall."
	waitkey
	append " Acrid, yet with a notable scent of artificial perfume. Odd."
	waitkey
	append " I approached the unattended counter and rang the bell, and quickly the same woman from the shops the other day emerged from the back with a broad smile."
	waitkey

	msg "\"You decided to give us a try?\" she asked."
	waitkey
	append "\nI nodded, but the smell was getting to me and I could feel a bad headache coming on already."
	waitkey
	append "\n\"Please wait over there\" she motioned to the seats, \"and I'll have someone take you in very soon. I hope you enjoy your new friend\"."
	waitkey
	append "\nAt those last few words, I could swear that smile got even wider."
	waitkey

	msg "At this point things get hazy."
	waitkey
	append " I couldn't have been waiting more than a few minutes, but the pain made it feel like hours as the headache rapidly set on my brain."
	waitkey
	append " There was a man whose name I don't recall"
	waitkey
	append " -- or maybe I never asked --"
	waitkey
	playsound "event:/Knocking"
	append " who led me into the back of the building that was lit surprisingly well."
	waitkey
	append " But the pain that shot through my eyes made it unbearable."
	waitkey
	append " I think the man smiled too, but how could he with this choking smell?"
	waitkey

	msg "There were creatures, sure."
	waitkey
	playsound "event:/Knocking"
	append " They howled and screamed and hollered incessantly, a nightmare house of strange furry shapes that didn't resemble anything I'd ever known as a pet."
	waitkey
	append " As we passed cages they writhed and chomped at the bars of their disconcertingly clean cages, and each guttural sound bit into the space behind my eyes like a hot iron brand striking flesh."
	waitkey

	bg wake
	msg "(It is at this point that Audrey ran out of time, as she spent half the week playing Alan Wake 2 instead of making this game."
	waitkey
	append " Some weeks are just game-playing weeks, not game-making weeks, you know how it is."
	waitkey
	append " At least Alan Wake 2 is very good)."
	waitkey

	msg "Oh, and one final thing... I opened the closet..."
	waitkey

	msg " "
	fadeto white 0.5
	wait 0.5
	bg tiger
	fadeto transparent 0.2
	wait 0.2

	playsound "event:/TigerMeow"
	msg "AHHHHHH"
	waitkey

	jump credits

:credits
	msg " "
	stopsound 0
	fadeto black 5
	justify left
	pos 16 32
	size 24
	wait 5

	msg "Thanks for playing!\nMusic: \"Lab Practicum\" from Half-Life 2\nSound Powered By FMOD Studio\n\nClick to Restart..."
	waitkey

	jump begin
